<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigehard of Aquileia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1077</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigehard was Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquileia">Aquileia</a> from 1068 to 1077. During the Investiture Controversy he supported Emperor Henry IV, who in 1077 rewarded him with the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>, followed soon after by Istria and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>. These grants laid the foundation of the patriarchs' temporal state, the Patria del Friuli. He died later that same year.</p></div>
